# FBE.7 — drop memory-graphiti from v0.1.0 first-run shape (M-FBM is the v0.1.0 floor)

2026-05-03. Luke's 2026-05-03 16:53 + 16:55 UTC ruling: graphiti
must NOT ship enabled in v0.1.0. M-FBM (file-based memory; built
at `framework/primary-persona/src/loam/primary_persona/file_memory.py`)
becomes the default memory backing for stranger-clone workspaces.
Direct Python calls into FileMemoryStore; no MCP server, no port,
no service.

Parent plan:
`docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-0-foldback-scope-expansion.md` §8 (FBE.7
backfilled post-FBE.2 by this amendment). Sub-plan:
`docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-0-foldback-scope-expansion-fbe7.md`.

Verified at planning (sub-plan §2 Surface #1): primary-persona's
production runtime ALREADY uses M-FBM. The remaining net work is
the workspace-bootstrap first-run scaffold:

  - `framework/workspace-bootstrap/src/loam/workspace_bootstrap/adapters/first_run_scaffold.py`:
    - `_SERVICE_KINDS` tuple: REMOVE `"memory-graphiti"` (line 223
      → 227-235 with FBE.7 provenance comments). Auto-launched set
      becomes `("orchestrator", "memory-write-worker")`.
    - `service_label`: docstring expanded; the `if kind not in
      _SERVICE_KINDS` guard now raises ValueError for
      `"memory-graphiti"`.
    - `_install_service_manager_files`: iteration switched from
      `_LAUNCHD_TEMPLATES.items()` to `_SERVICE_KINDS` so the
      retired graphiti template doesn't get written. The
      `_LAUNCHD_TEMPLATES["memory-graphiti"]` entry is preserved
      on disk (M-GMP re-admission shape).
    - `run_first_run_scaffold`: REMOVE the `_run_mcp_json_writer`
      invocation; replace with a literal `MCPJsonWriteResult(...,
      reason="skipped_v0_1_0_no_graphiti", path=None)`. The
      `_run_mcp_json_writer` helper itself stays in the tree
      (M-GMP + tests).
  - `framework/workspace-bootstrap/src/loam/workspace_bootstrap/adapters/mcp_json_writer.py`:
    - `MCPJsonWriteResult.path` widened from `Path` to `Path | None`
      (one-line type widening) to support the FBE.7 neutral-default
      construction. New reason value `"skipped_v0_1_0_no_graphiti"`
      documented in the docstring.

AC surface (per sub-plan §4):

  - AC.FBE.7.1 — `_SERVICE_KINDS` no longer contains
    `"memory-graphiti"`.
