  - AC.FBE.7.7 — negative AC: zero source edits to
    `framework/primary-persona/src/loam/primary_persona/`.
  - AC.FBE.7.8 — negative AC: zero edits to
    `framework/memory-system/`.
  - AC.FBE.7.9 — primary-persona tests pass 521/521 byte-identically.
  - AC.FBE.7.S — sealed-component fence: every diffed path is
    under `framework/workspace-bootstrap/` + universal-admissions.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - cli_memory_write in stop_emitter.py PRESERVED (sub-plan §2
    Surface #2 conflict-resolution): production runtime uses the
    queue → worker → FileBackedMemoryClient chain (which already
    satisfies "no MCP roundtrip in production"), and editing
    cli_memory_write would break the AC.J.8 + AC.M.10 + AC.J.2
    backwards-compat contracts that depend on
    build_live_mcp_memory_client being the patch site.
    Surface to the dispatcher in the FBE.7 status report so they
    can rule on whether AC #3's literal reading needs a corrective
    amendment.
  - mcp_json_writer kept entirely (sub-plan §2 Surface #3): the
    pure-function builders are the only callers M-GMP needs;
    deleting the writer would break AC47.2 + AC47.3 pure-function
    tests with no v0.1.0 benefit.
  - `_install_service_manager_files` iteration switched to
    `_SERVICE_KINDS` (sub-plan §2 Surface #4): the alternative of
    keeping graphiti in `_SERVICE_KINDS` and skipping its bootstrap
    was rejected — the plist file write IS the user-visible
    surface that says "graphiti is part of v0.1.0".

Out of scope (per sub-plan §8):

  - cli_memory_write source edit (Surface #2 ruling).
  - mcp_memory_client.py edits (dispatch hard constraint).
  - M-GMP plugin authoring.
  - Pos3 dev-workspace local cleanup.
  - framework/memory-system/ edits.

BASELINE a22272c (pre-apply tip; the FBE.7 source + test edits
commit). The workspace-bootstrap anchor's SEAL_COMMIT sidecar
lands at the seal SHA via `loam amend seal`.
